# Friends — Activity frontend AppSec

## MUST

- Treat all browser / SDK input as **attacker-controlled**.
- Avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; sanitize user answers if ever rendered as HTML.
- Secrets only on the server. `VITE_*` is public.
- Identity and scores from API after JWT — not from patched participant payloads alone.

## MUST NOT

- Put the Friends JWT in a durable store without XSS review (memory is the default).
- Redirect to an arbitrary URL from query params.

## SHOULD

- CSP compatible with Discord embed + SDK.
- No PII in analytics beyond the agreed privacy scope.
